  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0227 database is designed to manage information about airlines, airports, flights, and various related entities. The Airline table stores details about different airlines, including their names, headquarters locations, and logos. Each airport is represented in the Airport table, which includes its abbreviation, name, location, and radio operator, with the airport abbreviation serving as a foreign key referencing the AirportAbbreviation table. The AirportAirline table links airports with airlines, specifying the location where the airline operates from the airport. The Amenity table lists various amenities, such as food and beverage services, with a unique amenity name and code. The FlightCrew table stores information about the crew members, including their IDs and crew sizes. The FlightSchedule table contains details about flight schedules, including the flight number, airline name, departure and arrival times, crew ID, and origin and destination airports, with foreign keys referencing the Airline, FlightCrew, and Airport tables. The Model table lists different airplane models, including their names, manufacturers, and passenger capacities, with a composite primary key of model name and manufacturer. The Airplane table stores information about individual airplanes, including their tail numbers, airline names, model names, manufacturers, and nicknames, with foreign keys referencing the Airline and Model tables. The Role table lists different roles, such as pilot or flight attendant, and the CrewMember table stores information about individual crew members, including their FAA numbers, names, sexes, and roles, with a foreign key referencing the Role table. The FlightCrew_CrewMember table links crew members with their respective flight crews, specifying their roles. The Status table lists different statuses, such as on-time or delayed, and the FlightInstance table stores information about individual flight instances, including their IDs, flight numbers, tail numbers, statuses, departure dates and times, arrival times, and registered passenger numbers, with foreign keys referencing the FlightSchedule, Airplane, and Status tables. The ChargableInstance, AmenityChargableInstance, DomesticInstance, InternationalInstance, and LocalInstance tables are used to track various types of instances, such as chargeable instances, amenity instances, domestic instances, international instances, and local instances, with foreign keys referencing the FlightInstance table. The IncidentReport table stores information about incident reports, including incident IDs, flight instance IDs, reporter and reported FAA numbers, incident types, report times, and descriptions, with a foreign key referencing the FlightInstance table. The PersonnelReport table links incident reports with their respective sentiments, reported FAA numbers, and primary keys referencing the IncidentReport table.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project involves the development of a comprehensive airline management database system. The system tracks essential air travel information, including airlines, airports, flights, airplanes, crew members, and potential incidents. It caters to the operational needs of airlines and supports enhanced passenger services amidst evolving travel regulations and economic challenges.\n\nObjectives\n\n- To provide a robust system for managing airline operations, including flight scheduling, crew assignments, and airplane tracking.\n- To enhance operational efficiency by managing air travel logistics and incident reporting.\n- To support additional services and charges for domestic and local flights.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Airlines: Manage flight schedules, crew assignments, and billing for amenities.\n- Airport Operators: Facilitate flight route planning and coordinate with airlines.\n- Flight Crews: Report incidents and track flight schedules and roles.\n- Passengers: Use the services provided, although they are not direct users of the system.\n- Regulatory Bodies (e.g., FAA): Conduct background checks and ensure compliance.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Airline Management\n   - Record and manage airline details, headquarters, and associated airplanes.\n   - Track airplane models, manufacturers, and capacity.\n\n2. Airport Management\n   - Store and manage airport information, including abbreviation, name, and location.\n   - Handle airline operations at specific airports.\n\n3. Flight Scheduling and Instances\n   - Manage flight schedules, including origin, destination, departure, and arrival times.\n   - Track flight instances, including airplane assignment and number of registered passengers.\n\n4. Crew Management\n   - Assign and track flight crews, including roles and FAA verification.\n   - Record and manage crew member details and roles in flight schedules.\n\n5. Amenities and Charges\n   - Manage amenities offered and track charges for domestic and local flights.\n\n6. Incident Management\n   - Allow flight crew to report incidents occurring on flights.\n   - Generate incident reports and personnel reports, distinguishing between types of incidents.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Support increasing numbers of flights and crew without performance degradation.\n- Security: Ensure sensitive data, such as FAA numbers and incident reports, is securely managed.\n- Reliability: Maintain system uptime to support ongoing airline operations.\n- Compliance: Adhere to regulatory requirements for airline operations and crew validations.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0227.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0227\nCREATE TABLE `airline` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `headquarters` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `logo` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `airport` (\n  `abbreviation` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `radio_operator` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`abbreviation`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `airport_airline` (\n  `airport_abbreviation` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `airline_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`airport_abbreviation`, `airline_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `airport_airline_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`airport_abbreviation`) REFERENCES `airport` (`abbreviation`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `airport_airline_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`airline_id`) REFERENCES `airline` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `amenity` (\n  `code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `flight_crew` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `crew_size` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `flight_schedule` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `flight_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `airline_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `departure_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `arrival_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `crew_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `origin_airport` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `destination_airport` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_schedule_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`airline_id`) REFERENCES `airline` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_schedule_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`crew_id`) REFERENCES `flight_crew` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_schedule_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`origin_airport`) REFERENCES `airport` (`abbreviation`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_schedule_ibfk_4` FOREIGN KEY (`destination_airport`) REFERENCES `airport` (`abbreviation`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `model` (\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `manufacturer` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `passenger_capacity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`name`, `manufacturer`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `airplane` (\n  `tail_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `airline_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `model_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `manufacturer` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `nickname` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`tail_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `airplane_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`airline_id`) REFERENCES `airline` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `airplane_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`model_name`, `manufacturer`) REFERENCES `model` (`name`, `manufacturer`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `role` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `crew_member` (\n  `faa_number` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `sex` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`faa_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `crew_member_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `role` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `flight_crew_crew_member` (\n  `crew_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `crew_member_faa_number` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`crew_id`, `crew_member_faa_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_crew_crew_member_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`crew_id`) REFERENCES `flight_crew` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_crew_crew_member_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`crew_member_faa_number`) REFERENCES `crew_member` (`faa_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `status` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `flight_instance` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `flight_schedule_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `tail_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `status_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `departure_datetime` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `arrival_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `registered_passengers` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_instance_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`flight_schedule_id`) REFERENCES `flight_schedule` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_instance_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`tail_number`) REFERENCES `airplane` (`tail_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_instance_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`status_id`) REFERENCES `status` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `chargeable_instance` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `flight_instance_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `chargeable_instance_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`flight_instance_id`) REFERENCES `flight_instance` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `amenity_chargeable_instance` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `chargeable_instance_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `amenity_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `amenity_chargeable_instance_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`chargeable_instance_id`) REFERENCES `chargeable_instance` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `amenity_chargeable_instance_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`amenity_code`) REFERENCES `amenity` (`code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `domestic_instance` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `flight_instance_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `domestic_instance_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`flight_instance_id`) REFERENCES `flight_instance` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `international_instance` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `flight_instance_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `international_instance_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`flight_instance_id`) REFERENCES `flight_instance` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `local_instance` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `flight_instance_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `local_instance_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`flight_instance_id`) REFERENCES `flight_instance` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `incident_report` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `flight_instance_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `reporter_faa_number` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `reported_faa_number` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `incident_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `report_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `incident_report_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`flight_instance_id`) REFERENCES `flight_instance` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `personnel_report` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `incident_report_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sentiment` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `reported_faa_number` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `personnel_report_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`incident_report_id`) REFERENCES `incident_report` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
